.TH CHTTP_GET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_get \- do a GET request with the default client
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttp_get(const char *url,
                        chttpcli_response **resp_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This is a short wrapper. It makes a CHTTP_GET request for url. It runs
that request with the default client. It then frees the request.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
url       The target URL. It must not be NULL.
resp_out  It must not be NULL. The function sets it to NULL at once.
          If the call succeeds, it then gets the pointer to the
          response.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The same codes as chttpclient_do.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_post (3),
.BR chttp_put (3),
.BR chttp_delete (3),
.BR chttp_patch (3),
.BR chttp_do (3)
